WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.275
You might be surprised to learn that just plain

2
00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:08.925
being awake creates toxic products in your brain.

3
00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:12.030
How does the brain get rid of these poisons?

4
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.999
Turns out that when you sleep,

5
00:00:13.999 --> 00:00:16.285
your brain cells shrink.

6
00:00:16.285 --> 00:00:20.895
This causes an increase in the space between your brain cells.

7
00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:23.450
It's like unblocking a stream.

8
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:28.660
Fluid can flow past these cells and wash the toxins out.

9
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.240
So, sleep which can sometimes seem like such a waste of

10
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.970
time is actually your brain's way of keeping itself clean and healthy.

11
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.255
So, let's get right to a critical idea.

12
00:00:41.255 --> 00:00:45.770
Taking a test without getting enough sleep means you're operating with

13
00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:50.460
a brain that got little metabolic toxins floating around in it,

14
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.500
poisons, and make it so you can't think very clearly.

15
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.870
It's kind of like trying to drive a car that's got sugar in its gas tank,

16
00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.665
doesn't work too well.

17
00:00:59.665 --> 00:01:04.825
In fact, getting too little sleep doesn't just make you do worse on tests.

18
00:01:04.825 --> 00:01:09.560
Too little sleep over too long of a time can also be

19
00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:14.560
associated with all sorts of nasty conditions including headaches,

20
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.600
depression, heart disease, diabetes and just plain dying earlier.

21
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.175
But sleep does more than just allow your brain to wash away toxins.

22
00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:29.650
It's actually an important part of the memory and learning process.

23
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.545
It seems that during sleep,

24
00:01:31.545 --> 00:01:36.215
your brain tidies up ideas and concepts you're thinking about and learning.

25
00:01:36.215 --> 00:01:39.620
It erases the less important parts of memories and

26
00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:45.305
simultaneously strengthens areas that you need or want to remember.

27
00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.410
During sleep, your brain also rehearses

28
00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:51.450
some of the tougher parts of whatever you're trying to learn,

29
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:57.185
going over and over neural patterns to deepen and strengthen them.

30
00:01:57.185 --> 00:02:01.700
Sleep has also been shown to make a remarkable difference in your ability

31
00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.290
to figure out difficult problems and to understand what you're trying to learn.

32
00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:10.415
It's as if the complete deactivation of the conscious

33
00:02:10.415 --> 00:02:15.200
you in the prefrontal cortex at the forefront of your brain helps

34
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.955
other areas of your brain start talking more easily to one another

35
00:02:19.955 --> 00:02:21.965
allowing them to put together

36
00:02:21.965 --> 00:02:26.030
the neural solution to your learning task while you're sleeping.

37
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.700
Of course, you must also plant the seed for

38
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.190
your diffuse mode by first doing focused mode work.

39
00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.200
If you're going over what you're learning right before you

40
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.220
take a nap or going to sleep for the evening,

41
00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.730
you have an increased chance of dreaming about it.

42
00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.230
If you go even further and set it in mind that you want to dream about

43
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:52.400
the material it seems to improve your chances of dreaming about it, still further.

44
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:58.755
Dreaming about what you're studying can substantially enhance your ability to understand.

45
00:02:58.755 --> 00:03:04.525
It somehow consolidate your memories into easier to grasp chunks,

46
00:03:04.525 --> 00:03:09.080
and now, time for a little sleep.